      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "No. 237 is a two-bedroom mid-terrace residence situated on Larkhill Road, offering an excellent opportunity for refurbishment. Requiring complete modernisation and qualifying for the Vacant Property Refurbishment Grant, this property is sure to appeal to a wide range of purchasers.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation briefly comprises an entrance hallway leading to a kitchen/dining room and a separate living room. To the rear, doors open onto a generous south-east facing garden. Upstairs, there are two well-proportioned bedrooms and a main bathroom.\r\n\r\nLarkhill Road is a highly sought-after location, ideally positioned within walking distance of a range of local shops, schools, and cafés. The area is well serviced by public transport, with frequent bus routes and convenient access to the M1 and M50 motorways, as well as the Port Tunnel, providing swift connections to Dublin Airport and the city centre. Dublin City University and Omni Shopping Centre are both just a short 10-minute walk away.\r\n\r\nThis property presents an ideal opportunity for first-time buyers, investors, or those seeking a conveniently located home with significant potential.\r\n\r\nACCOMMODATION \r\n\r\nHallway: 1.77m x 2.78m\r\n\r\nLiving Room: 2.73m x 3.06m \r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room: 4.87m x 3.38m\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\n\r\nBedroom 1: 3.91m x 3.31m\r\n\r\nBedroom 2: 2.85m x 3.17m\r\n\r\nBathroom: 1.89m x 1.50m"
      },
